WHY TWO LICENCES.  The paper's claim that SEW-Bench is a "licence-free corpus" is a claim
about its *provenance*: the frames are synthesised by `annotation/generate_synthetic.py` from
a fixed seed and contain no third-party imagery, so nothing here is encumbered by an upstream
dataset agreement of the kind that gates HM3D, ScanNet, ScanNet++ or Ego4D. That is exactly
why an explicit outbound licence matters: provenance being clean is what makes it ours to
grant, and without a stated grant nobody could lawfully reuse it.

NOT COVERED.  The three natural-video benchmarks discussed in the paper (OpenEQA, VSI-Bench,
EgoSchema) and the registered EW-Bench design are not distributed here and are not covered by
this licence. EW-Bench requires habitat-sim plus an HM3D/ScanNet licence you must obtain
yourself; `annotation/generate_ewbench.py` is released up to its rendering call for that
reason.
